   *  dropped, but NOT YET written to the upsert below: GameMod.category is a
   *  single string tied to a small existing filter-chip vocabulary
   *  (Admin/Protection/Economy/Performance/Content/QoL/...) that 32,243 live
   *  Modrinth rows already populate with CATEGORY_LABEL[pt] and that the
   *  per-family chip UI (lib/mods-catalog.ts's listCategoryCounts) already
   *  reads from in production — overwriting it with Modrinth's own,
   *  differently-shaped category vocabulary needs a real schema decision
   *  (a new `categories String[]` column + a chip-UI change, or a mapping
   *  table), not a silent value swap in a bulk-write script. Left as a
   *  flagged follow-up rather than guessed at here. */
  categories?: string[];
};

