 * ever ran against real data): every regex below uses AT MOST ONE
 * variable-length quantifier between two fixed anchors (`&lt;tag` ... `&gt;`
 * or `&lt;/tag&gt;`). The ORIGINAL version chained several adjustable-length
 * pieces back to back — e.g. `\s+([^&]*?)\/?\s*&gt;` had `\s+`, a lazy
 * `[^&]*?`, and a trailing `\s*` all able to match the SAME run of space
